-- title:
--   Node pack at supersingular places over κ_A
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $\kappa_A = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ has characteristic $q$, and $N \ge 1$ with $q \nmid N$. The standing data are: `data`, a monic bivariate polynomial $\Phi$ of degree $\psi(q)$ killing the pair $(j, j_q)$, together with `hKr`, the congruence that its reduction modulo $q$ equals $(C X^{q} - X)(C X - X^{q})$; hypotheses `hα`, `hβ` that the two maps from the base-changed full level-$N$ function field to the full level-$Nq$ one over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, namely the inclusion and the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{q}$, are integral ring maps; `fm`, a fibre model of level $N$ over $A$ with constants $\kappa_A$ and reduction the residue map of $A$; `dataAll`, modular polynomial data for every divisor of $N$, with `hsep` asserting that the level-$N$ polynomial, reduced to $\kappa_A$ and viewed over $\kappa_A(X)$, is separable; `P`, a place specialization for these data, with `hP` saying that its map on places is the one attached to `fm`; and `R`, a prolongation tuple over `P` satisfying the fixed-place order law `OrderLawFixed`. Finally $w$ is a place of the level-$N$ function field $\kappa_A(j, j_N)$ which is supersingular (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set for $q$), and it is assumed that $w.\mathrm{ord}(j - j^{q^{2}}) = 1$ or $w.\mathrm{ord}(j_N - j_N^{q^{2}}) = 1$. The conclusion: for every finite extension $K/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ there is a finite extension $K'/\mathbb{Q}$ with $K \le K'$, node coordinates $c = (x,y)$ for $R$ over $K'$ at $w$, and $\varpi \in A \cap K'$, such that the ring $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K'\,w$ is local and Noetherian and: $\varpi$ generates the kernel of the reduction $A \cap K' \to \kappa_A$, i.e. $d$ reduces to $0$ iff $\varpi \mid d$; the maximal ideal of that ring is generated by the constant $\varpi$, by $c.x$ and by $c.y$; every $g$ in it has some $o \in A \cap K'$ with $g - o$ a non-unit; and for every such $g$, the first residue $R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_1\,w\,g$ is zero or has $w$-order $\ge 0$, while the second residue $R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2\,w\,g$ is zero or has order $\ge 0$ at the place $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\,q\,\kappa_A\,N \cdot w$ obtained by transporting $w$ along the coefficientwise Frobenius.
--
--   This is the local model of the level-$Nq$ curve at a supersingular point of the level-$N$ curve in characteristic $q$: the ring of functions regular on both branches is a two-dimensional local Noetherian ring whose maximal ideal is generated by a uniformiser of the constants together with coordinates $x$, $y$ cutting out the two branches, and residues along the two branches take integral values. It is used by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_commonUnit_pole_of_reduceFst_fixed_ordinary_residueField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_commonUnit_pole_of_reduceFst_fixed_ordinary_residueField) in the analysis of the reduction of the Hecke correspondence.
